From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:31:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: defer the ring kick while other requests are in
 flight

Each completed request group pushed its responses and notified the
front-end right away. Under load this makes the guest take one
interrupt per completion and fall into lockstep with tapdisk.

While at least kick_defer_max_held requests of the ring are in flight,
hold the push and the notification until kick_defer_max_held responses
are ready or a kick_defer_max_usecs deadline fires. With fewer requests
in flight the kick is sent immediately, so low queue depths are not
delayed.

tapback takes the settings of each VBD from the back-end keys
kick-defer-duration (microseconds, 0 disables the deferral) and
kick-defer-count, like polling-duration. Without them it uses 80 us and
8 responses. They reach tapdisk in the connect message. Counters are
exposed in the blkif stats under "kick_defer".

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
